> 3 3 2
3   Nu parni pāun.
3   Nu parnaš āškan šarraḫḫun.

2   Nu karimni pāun.

The tablet ends as the narrator enters the temple building itself. His disguise
and the fresh-baked bread must have been effective, as the next part of the
text begins with him in the inner sanctum, stolen god in hand.

